  "title": "A Georgia River Just Beat Its 1990 Flood Record #shorts",
  "description": "A flash flood emergency hit McCaysville, Georgia, and Copperhill, Tennessee, as the Toccoa River crested at a record 18.05 feet, above the 17.75 feet of 1990, according to gauge readings reported by local media. The Associated Press reports 3 to 5 inches of rain overnight; the Tennessee Valley Authority reported 8 to 10 inches in places. Dozens of people were rescued.\n\nSources: Associated Press, CNN, WSB-TV, FOX 5 Atlanta, National Weather Service, Tennessee Valley Authority (based on search-result excerpts). Gauge readings are preliminary; figures vary between reports; the rain area on the map is illustrative.\n\n#climate #weather #flood #georgia #tennessee",
